      "snapshot_index": 3,
      "player": "Gem25F Gramps",
      "decision_index": 5,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting a second creature (Hired Claw) in the precombat main phase when holding multiple combat tricks (Turn Inside Out, Full Bore, Might of the Meek) is suboptimal. The player should attack first with the existing Hired Claw to trigger its 'whenever you attack with one or more Lizards' ability for 1 damage, then potentially use combat tricks if needed. Deploying the second Hired Claw before combat gives the opponent information and doesn't help this turn's attack since the new creature has summoning sickness. More importantly, the player is tapping their only Mountain to cast the creature, leaving no mana open for combat tricks during the attack step. They could have attacked with the existing Hired Claw first (dealing 1 damage via trigger), then cast the second Hired Claw post-combat.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Hired Claw precombat, tapping the only Mountain, leaving no mana for combat tricks.",
      "better_line": "Attack with the existing Hired Claw first (triggering 1 damage to opponent, enabling the +1/+1 counter ability later), then cast the second Hired Claw in the post-combat main phase. This preserves the option to use a 1-mana combat trick during the attack if needed.",
