      "decision_index": 50,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Player incorrectly believed they had no blue mana available, but both Willowrush Verges can tap for U since they control a Forest. At 6 life facing two Hired Claws (which deal bonus damage via lizard attack triggers), an additional blocker is critical for survival. Mockingbird could have been cast for X=2-3 to copy a creature, while still potentially holding up Spider-Sense via web-slinging (returning a tapped creature to cast for just U).",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting anything, incorrectly reasoning they had no blue mana.",
      "better_line": "Cast Mockingbird using Willowrush Verge for U + additional lands for X, copying a relevant creature (like Hired Claw or Gene Pollinator) to get an additional blocker/threat, while keeping one land untapped and a tapped creature available for web-slinging Spider-Sense if needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 92,
      "player": "Gem25F Gramps",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "DSV3 Spike had lethal on board. Opponent is at 6 life. Attacking with both Hired Claws and Slickshot Show-Off would deal 2 damage from Hired Claw triggers, then casting any Turn Inside Out on Slickshot Show-Off (which also triggers Slickshot's +2/+0) would give massive flying damage - even one spell makes Slickshot a 6/2 flyer, totaling 10+ damage against 6 life. Instead, DSV3 Spike passed without casting spells or attacking, letting the opponent untap and attack them.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main without casting any spells, then apparently did not attack at all, completely missing lethal.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Slickshot Show-Off and both Hired Claws. Hired Claw triggers deal 2 damage. Cast Turn Inside Out on Slickshot Show-Off (becomes 6/2 flying). Combat damage of 6+1+1=8 plus 2 trigger damage = 10, which is lethal against opponent's 6 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 99,
      "player": "DSV3 Spike",
      "decision_index": 64,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "DSV3 Spike missed lethal damage. With Gem25F Gramps at 6 life, casting even one Turn Inside Out on the flying Slickshot Show-Off would make it a 6/2 (1+3 from Turn Inside Out +2 from Slickshot's noncreature spell trigger), dealing exactly 6 damage through the air with no flyers to block. Additional Hired Claw triggers and attacks would have added even more damage.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to cast any pump spells during combat",
      "better_line": "Cast Turn Inside Out targeting Slickshot Show-Off to deal 6 flying damage for lethal (or cast multiple pump spells for massive overkill)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 102,
      "player": "DSV3 Spike",
      "decision_index": 66,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 6 life facing lethal pressure from two Hired Claws (2 damage from triggers alone per attack) and a flying Slickshot Show-Off, Gramps passed without casting Mockingbird. A flying blocker copying Slickshot Show-Off (MV 2, so X=2, costing 3 mana total) would provide a crucial flying blocker while still potentially leaving mana for Spider-Sense via web-slinging. Without a blocker for the Slickshot, the opponent can freely attack with flying + pump spells for lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, leaving all mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast Mockingbird for X=2 (3 mana total) copying Slickshot Show-Off to get a 1/2 flying blocker. This blocks the opposing Slickshot and still allows holding up Spider-Sense via web-slinging (bouncing Mockingbird if needed) to counter pump spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 102,
      "player": "Gem25F Gramps",
      "decision_index": 65,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "DSV3 Spike is at 11 life, opponent is at 3 life. Both Hired Claws are tapped (they attacked), and Slickshot Show-Off is tapped (it attacked). DSV3 Spike has untapped Mountains and Fire Nation Palace. The Hired Claw ability says '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only if an opponent lost life this turn and only once each turn.' The opponent did lose life this turn (went from 6 to 3), so both Hired Claws can be activated to grow. But more critically, the opponent is at 3 life and DSV3 Spike has burn/pump spells in hand but no untapped attackers to target meaningfully for additional damage this combat. However, looking more carefully: Hired Claw has the triggered ability 'Whenever you attack with one or more Lizards, this creature deals 1 damage to target opponent' - both Hired Claws trigger, dealing 2 damage total. The opponent went from some life total to 3. Next turn, attacking with both Hired Claws would deal 2 (from triggers) + combat damage, easily killing the opponent at 3 life. But wait - the opponent has Gene Pollinators (1/2s) that could block. The key question is whether DSV3 Spike could have won THIS turn. With the opponent at 3 life after combat damage, and having Full Bore ({R}: +3/+2) and Turn Inside Out ({R}: +3/+0) in hand, plus 4 untapped lands producing red mana - but all creatures are tapped from attacking. There's no way to deal damage with pump spells on tapped creatures outside of combat. So passing seems reasonable... unless Fire Nation Palace's firebending ability could help, but that requires an attacking creature. Actually, re-reading: the opponent is at 3 life. DSV3 Spike passed without activating Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability. Both Hired Claws attacked, the opponent lost life, so the condition is met. Activating both Hired Claws ({1}{R} each) would make them 2/3s, which is relevant for getting through blockers next turn. With 3 untapped Mountains and Fire Nation Palace, DSV3 Spike has enough mana for at least one activation. Missing these activations when the opponent is at 3 life and has blockers available is a meaningful mistake.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating any Hired Claw +1/+1 counter abilities despite the opponent having lost life this turn and having available mana.",
      "better_line": "Activate both Hired Claws' +1/+1 counter abilities ({1}{R} each, 4 mana total with 3 Mountains + Fire Nation Palace available) to make them 2/3s, improving the ability to push through lethal damage next turn past the opponent's Gene Pollinator blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 109,
      "player": "DSV3 Spike",
      "decision_index": 71,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 3 life facing lethal on board (two Hired Claws deal 2 damage from triggers alone when attacking, plus combat damage), Gem25F Gramps declined to cast Mockingbird which could copy Spider Manifestation to create another blocker. With 8 lands/mana sources available, they could cast Mockingbird for X=2 (3 mana total) to copy Spider Manifestation, getting a 2/2 reach creature that also taps for mana. This additional blocker could be critical for surviving the next attack. At 3 life, every body on the battlefield matters for blocking, and passing with mana available and a creature in hand is wasteful when you're about to die.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, keeping Mockingbird and Spider-Sense in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Mockingbird for X=2 copying Spider Manifestation to get an additional 2/2 reach blocker. This helps survive the next attack phase while still holding up Spider-Sense (2 mana with web-slinging) to counter any combat tricks from the opponent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 112,
      "player": "Gem25F Gramps",
      "decision_index": 75,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "DSV3 Spike is at 11 life with the opponent at 3 life. The Slickshot Show-Off attacked this turn (it's tapped), and now in postcombat main, Spike has Full Bore and three Turn Inside Outs in hand with untapped Mountains and Fire Nation Palace. While there are no untapped creatures to target with pump spells right now (Slickshot and both Hired Claws are tapped), the decision to pass is technically correct since pump spells need a valid attack to matter. However, Spike could consider plotting a Slickshot Show-Off from hand (paying 1R) to set up a devastating next turn with plotted Slickshot + pump spells for lethal through the Spider Manifestation blocker. With opponent at 3 life, maximizing next turn's damage potential is critical. That said, the opponent has Spider-Sense potential (U open) and Spider Manifestation as a blocker with reach, so plotting to set up a bigger next turn could be the right call. Passing without plotting is slightly suboptimal.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without using any spells or abilities in postcombat main",
      "better_line": "Plot one of the Slickshot Show-Offs (paying 1R from untapped Mountains) to guarantee two Slickshots next turn, enabling a lethal alpha strike with pump spells through the Spider Manifestation blocker",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "DSV3 Spike",
      "decision_index": 80,
    }
  ],
